From a097adcb4b91f1b605ec6065ac1b6890d6487615 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dfattal <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:00:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 63/64] inline-3d(Phase 2): build the plane split, leave it
 inert
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 2 lifts the page content that sits OVER a woven inline-3D tile onto its
own transparent plane, so the display processor can composite it above the weave
instead of the page burying the tile. This patch builds every piece of that and
deliberately wires none of it up: with --inline-3d-occlusion off (the default)
nothing runs at all, and with it on an extra transparent surface is produced and
ignored. Presented pixels are unchanged either way.

The split is computed at DRAW time from the live root quad_list, never from the
aggregation-time quad ordinals in AggregatedFrame — those are invalidated before
drawing by Display::RemoveOverdrawQuads() and OverlayProcessor::ProcessForOverlays(),
both of which erase and reorder quads.

Ordering, stated once so it stays stated: QuadList index 0 is the FRONTMOST quad
(painted last, appears on top); the draw loop walks BackToFrontBegin() == rbegin.
So for a tile canvas quad at index k, the OVER set is [0, k) and back-to-front is
descending index.

  * DirectRenderer::ComputeInline3dPlaneSplit walks the root pass once, finds
    each tile's k by canvas resource id (LAST match wins — the deepest
    occurrence, the widest defensible over set), and records the tile rect on
    every quad in front of it that intersects it. Per-quad clip vectors: a quad
    above tile A and below tile B is clipped against A only. A tile whose k
    cannot be found keeps Phase-1 behaviour and logs (R1).
  * Excluded from the over set, each counted by reason: 3D sorting contexts,
    non-kSrcOver blends, ALL AggregatedRenderPassDrawQuads (pixel-moving filters
    exist — "it only wraps one pass" is false), RequiresOverlay quads, any
    registered tile's own canvas quad, and resources already suppressed from the
    page draw.
  * SkiaRenderer::MaybeDrawInline3dOverPlane paints that set into a lazily
    allocated window-sized non-scanout premul RGBA8 plane, using the root pass's
    target-to-device transform so a quad lands in identical device pixels, and
    publishes the mailbox via SkiaOutputSurface::SetInline3dOverPlane. Painted
    before the root pass, so the GPU task queue is strictly plane-then-page (R7);
    is_overlay=false keeps MaybeWeaveRootRenderPass inert for it and it never
    enters the pass list (R8). The GPU side stores the mailbox and size and reads
    them nowhere.
  * The difference clip that would punch the page out of the tiles is fully
    plumbed (per-quad vectors, batch flush on transition, the kDifference loop in
    PrepareCanvas) but gated off by inline3d_difference_clip_enabled_ = false.
    That single bool is what patch 0064 flips. The batch flush is gated on the
    clip actually being applied, because breaking a batch would perturb Skia's
    inter-quad AA seams and that would be observable.
  * Diagnostics for hardware verification, throttled ~1-in-60, marker
    "[DisplayXR] inline-3D plane-split:": per-tile k, over-set size, and the
    excluded-by-reason tallies.

Display now feeds the renderer {rect, canvas resource id, element identity} per
tile; the geometry-only SetInline3DRects feed the mac overlay-substitution path
consumes is left exactly as it was. AggregatedFrame::Inline3dTrackedRect carries
the SharedQuadState layer id + namespace through from the aggregator, so a later
patch can key k by identity instead of by resource id.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
